      "findingMessages": {
        "p0012-correctness-corpus-pngsuite-never-downloaded": "`cargo xtask corpus` documents that --download fetches PngSuite and CC0 raw samples, and crates/codecs/tests/corpus.rs says corpus/pngsuite is fetched by that command, but cmd_corpus only iterates RAW_SAMPLES into corpus/raw. corpus/pngsuite is never created, so corpus_pngsuite (including the never-panic check on deliberately corrupt x* PNGs) silently skips on every machine and CI run that relies on the documented download, leaving PNG decoder corpus coverage permanently unexercised while appearing to pass.",
        "p0012-correctness-static-check-substring-contracts": "The desktop CI gate's 'static contracts' step reports bounded IPC/cache/stale-preview contracts as enforced by checking only that source files contain identifier substrings (sync_channel, MAX_JS_SAFE_ID, MAX_PENDING, DEFAULT_TTL, descriptor.sequence, MAX_SLICE = 512). A change that removes the bound enforcement while keeping the constant name or a comment mentioning it still prints 'desktop static contract: PASS (... IPC/cache contracts)', so the gate claims behavioural guarantees it never exercises (false coverage)."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "p0012-correctness-corpus-pngsuite-never-downloaded": "Add PngSuite (pinned URL + sha256) to cmd_corpus --download, or correct the usage text and corpus.rs header and make the PNG corpus test fail rather than skip where coverage is expected.",
        "p0012-correctness-static-check-substring-contracts": "Replace the substring checks with behavioural tests that exercise the bounds (queue capacity, id range, cache eviction, stale-sequence rejection), or relabel the step as a presence lint so it is not counted as contract coverage."
      },
